Reason: 1result.sql correctly unnests the per‑alternate VEP annotations with UNNEST(ab.vep), so each consequence is matched to the corresponding alternate base. 2result.sql refers to UNNEST(vep) outside the alternate_bases struct (and requires v.allele = 'T'), which does not exist at that level and would fail or give no rows. Thus 1result.sql is the valid query that fulfils the task.